AUDIO: 'Hello! In this video I\'ll show you how to work with LTX Director and the Sulphur2 model (a modified LTX 2.3), fp8 and bf16 are essentially different models: fp8 is a compressed version, lighter on resources, but the results are worse.'

[00:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Starting the bundle.'

[00:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Alright, the bundle is ready to go. Opening ComfyUI.'

[00:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'On every launch this workflow is installed straight from the developer\'s GitHub, so you always work with the latest version of LTX Director.'

[01:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is the main node, where all the work happens.'

[01:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It\'s better to test generation on a short time span first, so you don\'t have to wait long. Then, if needed, put all the prompts and settings together and generate the whole video. Split your prompts into short time intervals — the model generates more accurately that way. You have to tune the video duration so that what you planned has time to happen without being slowed down. With the wrong duration, the model can hallucinate.'

[01:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ll go through several ways to generate.'

[01:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Alright, I\'ll start with generating video from an image First, I\'ll show you how to make a person in a photo say the text we need I\'ve already prepared the images and prompts, so we don\'t waste time now on the trial and error you\'ll definitely face when working from scratch for real'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Adding the image Writing the prompt'

[02:16] [scene:talk]
